0F (18\u201327 \u00b0C) and humidity 41\u201366%, 80 \u00b0F (27 \u00b0C) and 41% at 11:52 AM. Water 74 \u00b0F (23.1 \u00b0C) at CDIP 191."],["Swell","CDIP 191 at 11:00 AM: 15.4 s from S 191\u00b0, 4.6 ft (1.41 m); 12.5 s from WNW 282\u00b0, 2.8 ft (0.86 m). At 5:00 AM: 15.4 s from S 190\u00b0, 4.1 ft (1.24 m); 14.3 s from W 272\u00b0, 2.9 ft (0.87 m). Breaking at 11:00 AM, against 5:00 AM: North 5.2 ft (1.59 m), little change; Center 3.6 ft (1.11 m), little change; South 3.7 ft (1.12 m), little change. North leads, as it did. Arriving at all three breaks: the 15.0 s train from the Southern Ocean, sent about Oct 9 from about 6,500 mi (10,000 km) away, about 14 s by 11:00 PM."],["Tide","The tide is pushing to 5.5 ft (1.67 m) at 4:56 PM then dropping to 2.0 ft (0.60 m) at 12:08 AM tomorrow. The previous AM low was 4.4 ft (1.33 m) at 11:30 AM. The gauge is running 1.3 ft (0.39 m) over the harmonic prediction, over the last 3 days. Today's range is 1.1 ft (0.34 m), neap tides; springs around Oct 25. On the 2016 survey the tide moves where the waves break, not how big they are; this season's sandbars are not known."],["Wind","W 270\u00b0 at 8 mph (7 kt) at 11:52 AM: cross-shore at North; onshore at Center and South. At this hour on the 31 days before: North cross-shore on 12; Center onshore on 14, cross-shore on 15; South onshore on 18. Median 9 mph (8 kt)."],["Watching","Tropical Storm [Trudy](https://www.nhc.noaa.gov/archive/2026/TRUDY_graphics.php) {tropical storm symbol}: every fix NHC has logged or forecast is behind land from Point Loma South, so nothing it has sent reaches the breaks."]]}}